# research.local.env.example
#
# Copy this file to `research.local.env` (same directory, the repository root) and edit it.
# `research.local.env` is git-ignored: it names a path on ONE machine, which is exactly the thing
# this repository must not carry. This example is committed; the real file never is.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FRB_WATERFALLS -- the root of the CHIME/FRB Catalog 1 waterfall tree
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The figures under `research/figures` run on:
#
#     CHIME/FRB Catalog 1 waterfalls
#     CHIME/FRB Collaboration 2021, ApJS 257, 59 (arXiv:2106.04352)
#     public release CANFAR CISTI.CANFAR/21.0007
#
# That is a SEPARATE PUBLIC DOWNLOAD, cited on its own terms. It is not part of this repository,
# no script here fetches it, and it is far too large to ship. Obtain it yourself from CANFAR.
#
# Point FRB_WATERFALLS at the directory that CONTAINS the per-event directories -- the root of the
# tree, not one event -- so that `<root>/*/*_waterfall.h5` matches:
#
FRB_WATERFALLS=/path/to/chime-frb-catalog1
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Precedence
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Most specific first:
#
#   1. an explicit argument, which still works and still wins:
#          python research/figures/frb_panel.py /other/tree
#   2. the environment variable of the same name, for a single run:
#          FRB_WATERFALLS=/other/tree python research/figures/frb_panel.py
#   3. this file, written once per machine.
#
# If none is set there is NO fallback: the scripts refuse, and say so. That is deliberate. These
# scripts write committed artifacts (`frb_panel.csv`, `frb_spotcheck.csv`), so a path that resolves
# to nothing would overwrite a good table with an empty one while still exiting 0.
